      <img src="/media/marker.jpg" class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-box object-cover lg:col-span-5">
      <div class="self-center lg:col-span-7">
        <blockquote class="first-line text-[clamp(1.625rem,1.9vw+1rem,2.625rem)] leading-[1.24]"><p>Most people who come to me already have the essay. They&rsquo;ve been telling it at dinner for ten years. We slow it down until it&rsquo;s on the page.</p></blockquote>
        <p class="body-copy measure mt-8">I wrote for daily papers in Maine and Vermont for fourteen years, a feature by Thursday and a column by Saturday, and I was good at being quick. Then I taught the personal essay to people who came in from work at seven in the evening, and I learned what happens when nobody is in a hurry.</p>
        <p class="body-copy measure mt-4">This course is those evenings, made smaller. Fourteen people, one essay each, and I read every draft twice.</p>
        <p class="title-small mt-8">Hollis Ouellette</p>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">who teaches The Slow Draft</p>
        <p class="mt-6"><a href="/about" class="link-mark font-semibold">About Hollis</a></p>
      </div>
